ydroxyl ate dopamine into a  different location so here you can see  there is a hydroxylation reaction on the  dopamine and this hydroxylation reaction  would ultimately give rise to  norepinephrine and remember  norepinephrine and epinephrine that  means actually nor noradrenaline these  are actually important neurotransmitters  in let's say postganglionic nerve fibers  of sympathetic nervous system so from  norepinephrine epinephrine would be  produced so you can see this phenyl  ethyl or ethanolamine and methyl  transferase which actually transfers a  methyl group onto this a mind group of  epinephrine or epinephrine would  ultimately produce this epinephrine so  these epinephrine norepinephrine and  dopamine work individually as  neurotransmitters but remember all of  these are descended from phenylalanine  which is a amino acid so any disease  which corresponding to loss of  neurotransmitter may actually involved  with this pathway so let's talk about  the serotonin biosynthesis pathway so  the serotonin the raw material for  serotonin is tryptophan tryptophan is an  aromatic amino acid so it has a double  ring attached with it one  ben turmeric and another is hexameric so  first reaction is also hydroxylation  reaction that means addition of a  hydroxyl group by tryptophan hydroxylase  enzyme and it would form five dihydroxy  tryptophan or five DHT and five  dihydroxy tryptophan would be  decarboxylated by decarboxylase enzyme  and it would produce serotonin which is  a biologically active and mine you can  see it's a mine it's lived with these of  aromatic group with the hydroxylated end  it would produce serotonin so in this  video we discussed about the basic  biochemical pathways of biogenesis of  serotonin epinephrine norepinephrine and  dopamine in another video I would talk  about glutamate biosynthesis and how  glutamate is used as a neurotransmitter  and also about clear mate transporters I  hope you enjoyed this video if you liked  my video give it a